  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Oral heroic epic of Mongolia, recited by the tuulch, an epic singer, in performances of hundreds to thousands of lines that combine praise, benedictions and tales of heroes, and inscribed on UNESCO's List of Intangible Cultural Heritage in Need of Urgent Safeguarding. The tradition survives chiefly among the Oirat groups of western Mongolia, where the tuulch accompanies the recitation on the tovshuur, often in a deep, guttural voice; the repertoire comprises many epics besides the Jangar cycle.",
